Key Systems
Card System

The card system uses reusable C# data structures to define card effects, display information, and gameplay behavior. This structure makes it easier to add new cards without rewriting the core combat logic.

Combat System

The combat system manages player actions, enemy responses, damage resolution, debuffs, and battle feedback. Combat results are displayed through a dedicated combat log system.

Enemy System

Enemy behavior and enemy data are separated into different scripts. This makes enemy configuration easier to manage and extend.

Save System

The global save manager handles persistent game data and reset behavior. This supports testing, replayability, and player progression.

Event System

The event system supports branching choices and roguelike-style progression. Event data is separated from core game logic to improve maintainability.

